the nevada family is pleading for the  safe return of a 15-year-old girl  tonight nomie armand deres was last seen  yesterday morning at her home on the  paiute reservation just outside of las  vegas and now those who love the teen  just want to bring her home safely sasha  loftus spoke with nomi's family tonight  and she's in our newsroom with more  denise and bryant nomie's family says  they just want her back they're calling  on the community but they're also  speaking to the teen herself saying they  won't give up until she's found  it's been a  living nightmare nearly two days since  she was last seen  the family of nomi armandaris is  pleading for her to come home when we  wake up we think of her when we go to  sleep she's the last thing we think  about nomi's sister evangelia tapia says  the 15 year old left her home here on  the paiute reservation tuesday around 5  a.m to go to school and she's been  missing ever since someone's influencing  her to do this someone's telling her  what to do tapia and nomi's uncle nino  alvarez call this out of character and  they're terrified she's with someone  else ultimately in danger she didn't  give us any kind of sign that this was  going to happen that's why they're  calling on las vegas and all of southern  nevada to come forward with any  information that could help  but more than anything they hope to  speak to nomi herself you just tell us  that you're scared  and that you  that you want us to come get you and  we'll come get you to remind her how  much they love her  and how they don't want to face any kind  of future  without her tell me just please come  home  nomi is five foot two with brown eyes  and black and red hair if you have seen  her if you have any information you are  asked to call the paiute police  department at 702-471-0844  or the las vegas fbi we have more  information on our website  8newsnow.com reporting in the newsroom  tonight sasha loftis live local now
 

